Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||10-02-1999||05:08 PM||||i have an '86 SE 2M6 and when i start it while cold, it has to either warm up for a while or be revved way up to get it into gear. it also overheats, and idles at 1500-2000 rpm. could all of this be caused by my coolant temperature sensor? the only error code i get besides 12 is 15, and thats coolant temperature sensor. any help is appreciated! (p.s. the car is a manual)||||reg||1
Z||000001||mwbackus||10-02-1999||06:07 PM||||Do you mean you actually cannot shift into a gear until it warms up, etc. or that it just kills starting off while its cold?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||10-02-1999||06:23 PM||||I have heard that the coolant temp sensor will cause the car to not run or run poorly.  If you are getting the sensor error code by all means replace it.  (i dont know off hand what 1-5 is.<BR>as far as overheating, did you play with your timing?  i thought that the collant temp sensor just adjusted the fuel/air mixture, and not the timing, but i could be wrong.<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 10-02-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero64||10-03-1999||10:57 AM||||The coolant temp sensor will definately cause the problems you are having.  The sensor is relatively cheap if bought thru AutoZone or a comparable outlet and should be replaced if you are getting a trouble code for that part of the system.  Replace the sensor and chances are that most if not all of your symptoms will go away....Good luck ||||reg||6
